.TH ckman-oath-accounts-code 1  ckman 
.SH NAME
ckman\-oath\-accounts\-code \- Generate codes from matching accounts using each account\*(Aqs own period. Touch\-protected TOTP accounts request touch individually. HOTP accounts are calculated only when exactly one account matches. Results are printed as each account completes
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBckman\-oath\-accounts\-code\fR [\fB\-s\fR|\fB\-\-single\fR] [\fB\-H\fR|\fB\-\-show\-hidden\fR] [\fB\-p\fR|\fB\-\-password\fR] [\fB\-\-remember\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fIQUERY\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Generate codes from matching accounts using each account\*(Aqs own period. Touch\-protected TOTP accounts request touch individually. HOTP accounts are calculated only when exactly one account matches. Results are printed as each account completes
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-s\fR, \fB\-\-single\fR
Ensure only a single match, and output only the code
.TP
\fB\-H\fR, \fB\-\-show\-hidden\fR
Include hidden accounts
.TP
\fB\-p\fR, \fB\-\-password\fR \fI<PASSWORD>\fR
The password to unlock the OATH application
.TP
\fB\-\-remember\fR
Remember the password on this machine (long\-only: the global \-r/\-\-reader owns the short flag)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
[\fIQUERY\fR]
Query string to match specific accounts
